FAQ = [
 ("What is the best trailer hitch for a Jeep Wrangler JL?",
  "For most JL owners, the CURT 13392. It is a Class III hitch with a 2 in receiver rated 5,000 lb gross trailer weight and 500 lb tongue weight, it bolts to existing frame points, and its 9 in receiver tube helps a hitch bike rack clear the tailgate spare. etrailer lists it at $126.38. CURT excludes the EcoDiesel. If you want the factory part instead, the Mopar 82215209 is a Class 2 receiver rated 3,500 lb."),
 ("How much can a Jeep Wrangler JL tow?",
  "It depends on body style, powertrain and model year. Dealer towing guides list 2,000 lb for the 2018–2023 2-door and 3,500 lb for the 2018–2023 4-door. For 2024 and later, properly equipped 4-door models with the 3.6L V6 or 2.0L turbo and the 8-speed automatic are listed at 5,000 lb, and 2-doors at 3,500 lb. The 4xe and Rubicon 392 are listed at 3,500 lb in every year. Confirm your exact figure in the owner's manual or Jeep's towing guide."),
 ("Does a Class III hitch raise my Wrangler's towing capacity?",
  "No. The hitch rating and the vehicle rating are separate limits, and the lower one always applies. A 5,000 lb CURT hitch on a 2020 2-door still leaves you at 2,000 lb, because that is what Jeep rates the vehicle for. A Class III hitch is still useful on a JL: the 2 in receiver takes most bike racks and cargo carriers, and it gives a 4-door on the 2024+ rating room to use the full 5,000 lb."),
 ("Did my JL come with a factory hitch?",
  "Only if it was ordered with the Trailer Tow package. Look under the rear bumper for a square receiver bolted to the frame, and check the window sticker. Owners on JLwranglerforums report that the factory receiver they have seen on the JL is a Class II rated 3,500 lb. If a receiver is already there, you only need wiring and a ball mount; if not, any hitch on this page bolts on."),
 ("Will a hitch bike rack hit the Wrangler's spare tire?",
  "It can. The JL carries its spare on the tailgate, so a platform or hanging rack has to reach past it. A longer receiver tube helps: CURT's 13392 uses a 9 in tube, which etrailer notes is meant to help bike racks clear the spare. Many owners also add a hitch extender or a rack with a tilting arm. Measure from the receiver pin hole to the back of the tire before you order a rack."),
 ("Do these hitches fit the Wrangler 4xe?",
  "The 4xe uses the same JL frame points as other Wranglers, and Quadratec's Q&A confirms the Mopar 82215209 on 4xe models. CURT's 13392 listing excludes only the EcoDiesel. The 4xe tow rating stays at 3,500 lb regardless of the hitch. For the budget listings, confirm the 4xe with the seller before buying, since their fitment notes are thinner."),
 ("Does a Wrangler hitch work with a steel aftermarket bumper?",
  "Often not. The hitches here bolt to the frame behind the factory rear bumper. Many aftermarket steel rear bumpers either include their own 2 in receiver or cover the frame points these hitches use. If you have or plan a steel bumper, check whether it has a built-in receiver first; if it does, you don't need a separate hitch. If it doesn't, ask the bumper maker which hitches it clears."),
 ("What wiring do I need to tow with a JL?",
  "A 4-way flat connector handles tail, brake and turn lights, which covers most small utility trailers and hitch-mounted lights. For a trailer with electric brakes you need a 7-way connector and a brake controller. None of the hitches here include a harness except bundles like the WeiSen kit. Budget for a vehicle-specific plug-in harness, which clips into the JL's taillight connectors without splicing."),
 ("How long does it take to install a Wrangler JL hitch?",
  "Draw-Tite quotes 20 minutes for its 76382, and CURT rates the 13392 as a novice-level install. Quadratec lists the Mopar receiver at under an hour with no drilling or bumper removal. The CURT instructions call for temporarily lowering the exhaust to get the hitch into place, and a few etrailer reviewers mention drilling for bolt clearance, so allow extra time and have a torque wrench on hand."),
 ("Is a 1.25 in receiver enough for a Wrangler?",
  "It works for a light bike rack, but on a JL the 2 in receiver is the better choice. Every hitch on this page uses a 2 in opening, which takes the widest range of platform racks, cargo carriers and ball mounts. A 2 in receiver also matches the factory Mopar part, so accessories swap between Jeeps without adapters."),
]

